@namespace Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor

@* The kildeutforsker whole: the kilde list, the drill-in, and the open kilde in the host's address
   bar. (Fhi.Metadata-zrcf4, Fhi.Metadata-8uwtd)

   Deliberately far smaller than VariableExplorer, and that is Kelda's contract rather than a
   shortcut: KildeSearch has no SearchChanged and no pager, so search, filters and column choices
   are component state that goes away on refresh. What is worth putting in a URL is which kilde is
   open and which order the list is in.

   ?search= is not read, for that same reason — a link carrying it would work exactly once and
   could not be shared onward. It is left in the address bar rather than erased, along with
   everything else this component does not own.

   ?datasamling= is read beside ?kilde= rather than instead of it, so the drill-in from a kilde to
   one of its datasamlinger is an address that names the whole path: a link opens the datasamling,
   and Back leaves the kilde behind it.

   @key is _arrival, the count of addresses that arrived under a standing circuit, so a press a
   host's Router intercepted remounts the component that reads its query at initialisation. Keyed
   on the count and not on the ids: opening a kilde from the list moves those without a navigation,
   and remounting there would throw away the list the reader pressed in.

   No @page and no @rendermode, like everything else here; but this one owns the query string, so
   it must be mounted interactively. No class names and no markup of its own. *@

<KildeSearch @key="_arrival"
             SelectedKildeId="@_selectedKildeId"
             SelectedKildeIdChanged="@KildeChanged"
             SelectedDatasamlingId="@_selectedDatasamlingId"
             DatasamlingHref="@DatasamlingHref"
             @bind-Order="_order"
             ExploreVariablesRequested="@Handover"
             Language="@Language"
             ShowAccessAndPrices="@ShowAccessAndPrices" />
